     "citations": null,
     "text": "{\"completeness\": 0.65, \"citation_quality\": 0.3, \"severity_defensibility\": 0.75, \"overall_pass\": false, \"feedback\": \"The investigation appropriately downgrades severity from high to medium based on zero confidence findings and lack of corroborating evidence, which is well-defended. However, there are two significant gaps: (1) No ATT&CK techniques are cited despite this being an identity compromise scenario\u2014techniques like T1078 (Valid Accounts), T1556 (Modify Authentication Process), or T1110 (Brute Force) would be relevant if compromise were suspected, and their absence or explicit rejection would strengthen the analysis; (2) The completeness is undermined by not addressing the alert routing's claim about 'classic identity and authentication risk'\u2014the investigation should explicitly validate or refute this characterization and explain why geolocation-based detection alone is insufficient. The recommended actions are sound (user contact, log verification, escalation criteria), but the investigation needs deeper ATT&CK mapping and more explicit reasoning about why impossible travel alone doesn't trigger higher techniques or severity without authentication log confirmation.\"}",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
