 "8996322c4d8c1600": [
  {
   "container": null,
   "content": [
    {
     "citations": null,
     "text": "{\"attack_techniques\":[],\"identity_signals\":{\"impossible_travel\":false,\"mfa_fatigue\":false,\"privilege_escalation\":false,\"dormant_account_reactivation\":false,\"notes\":\"Alert triggered on impossible_travel pattern (127 minutes between New York and Tokyo), but identity investigation found no corroborating evidence in auth logs. Zero confidence in the alert authenticity.\"},\"key_findings\":\"An impossible travel alert was generated for user jlee between New York and Tokyo with only 127 minutes transit time. However, the identity investigation found no supporting evidence in authentication logs and assigned zero confidence to the alert, suggesting this is likely a false positive or alert source misconfiguration. Direct verification with the user and identity provider logs is essential before escalation.\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"severity_rationale\":\"While the alert describes an impossible travel pattern (which would normally indicate high-severity account compromise), the identity investigation detected zero confidence in the finding with no supporting evidence in auth logs. The alert has not been validated as a real sign-in event. This appears to be either a false positive from the monitoring system or unverified telemetry. As an unconfirmed account anomaly with no evidence of actual compromise or successful unauthorized access, this falls into medium severity\u2014a potential attack that controls or detection gaps may have failed to validate, but without confirmed internal impact.\",\"confidence\":0.0,\"recommended_response\":\"1. Immediately verify the alert source (InsightIDR) for configuration errors or data quality issues. 2. Contact jlee directly to confirm whether they traveled to Tokyo and authenticate the legitimacy of any sign-in attempts during the alleged impossible travel window. 3. Query identity provider logs directly (Okta, Azure AD, etc.) to confirm whether any authentication events exist for this user during the timeframe\u2014if none exist, the alert is a false positive. 4. If authentication events are confirmed, escalate to high severity and initiate account security review; if not, suppress the alert and investigate the sensor misconfiguration.\",\"rounds_used\":0}",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "diagnostics": null,
   "id": "msg_011Ch9y2A9KTvp5KKpGaLV9a",
   "model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001",
