  {
   "container": null,
   "content": [
    {
     "citations": null,
     "text": "{\"attack_techniques\":[],\"identity_signals\":{\"impossible_travel\":false,\"mfa_fatigue\":false,\"privilege_escalation\":false,\"dormant_account_reactivation\":false,\"notes\":\"Alert claims impossible travel (127 minutes between New York and Tokyo), but identity investigation found no corroborating evidence. Recommended actions include verifying alert source and contacting user directly.\"},\"key_findings\":\"An impossible travel alert was triggered for user jlee between New York and Tokyo with a 127-minute time delta. However, identity system investigation found no supporting evidence in authentication logs and returned zero confidence (0.0), suggesting the alert may be a false positive or based on unreliable geolocation data. Direct user contact and identity provider log verification are needed to confirm the alert's validity.\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"severity_rationale\":\"While the alert describes an anomalous sign-in pattern (impossible travel), the identity investigation found zero confidence and no corroborating evidence in authentication logs. The alert appears to originate from geolocation inference rather than confirmed malicious activity or confirmed unauthorized access. Without evidence of actual compromise, internal host impact, or successful account takeover, this does not meet the threshold for high severity. This is a medium-severity suspected false positive requiring validation.\",\"confidence\":0.1,\"recommended_response\":\"Contact jlee directly to confirm their actual location and travel plans during the flagged time window. Query the identity provider's authentication logs independently to verify login timestamps and source IPs. If the user confirms legitimate travel or the logs show no actual authentication event, close as false positive. If the user denies the travel or activity, escalate to incident response for account compromise investigation including password reset, MFA review, and session review.\",\"rounds_used\":0}",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
