     "citations": null,
     "text": "{\"completeness\": 0.85, \"citation_quality\": 0.4, \"severity_defensibility\": 0.75, \"overall_pass\": false, \"feedback\": \"The investigation demonstrates strong completeness with thorough recommended actions and logical reasoning about false positive potential. However, it critically fails on citation quality by citing zero ATT&CK techniques despite this being a clear identity compromise scenario\u2014impossible travel is a hallmark of T1078 (Valid Accounts) abuse and potentially T1550 (Use Alternate Authentication Material). The severity assessment is somewhat defensible given the lack of corroborating evidence, but downgrades an impossible travel alert to medium without sufficient justification; even unconfirmed impossible travel should typically remain high severity pending verification, as the absence of evidence in one log source doesn't eliminate the risk. To pass, explicitly map this to relevant ATT&CK techniques (T1078, T1550, T1556 if MFA bypass is suspected), and reconsider whether medium severity is appropriate for an unvalidated but structurally plausible impossible travel pattern\u2014the investigation should acknowledge that some high-severity alerts genuinely lack immediate log confirmation but still warrant urgent verification rather than downgrade.\"}",
